    "citations": null,
    "text": "{\"completeness\": 0.9, \"citation_quality\": 0.85, \"severity_defensibility\": 0.9, \"overall_pass\": true, \"feedback\": \"This is a strong triage submission that meets the standard for escalation. The analyst correctly identified three relevant ATT&CK techniques with solid justification\u2014T1059.001 for PowerShell command execution, T1105 for the download intent, and T1027 for obfuscation techniques. The key findings accurately describe the malicious indicators present in the command line, and the severity assessment is well-reasoned and appropriately bounded (high rather than critical, with clear explanation of what would elevate it further). The recommended response is comprehensive and prioritizes containment before investigation. Minor areas for enhancement: explicitly documenting whether network controls (IDS/proxy) blocked the connection would strengthen the initial assessment, and noting the MD5 hash validity/reputation check would add one more data point, but these are not critical gaps given the clear malicious intent evident in the command itself.\"}",
    "type": "text"
   }
  ],
